Z||000000||85fierogt||08-29-2001||04:19 PM||||this is gonna make me sound really reatrded but i just got my performance ocelot exhaust from the fiero store and i ant to make sure i do this right, i havnt even opened the box yet but i was wondering if someone could list the steps to install the exhaust system, thanks<BR>-brad<P>hey its how you learn||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||08-29-2001||04:37 PM||||1) open box<BR>2) pull out of box<BR>3) check to make sure the inlet side is a compression fiting with the proper clamps.. if not reverse 1 and 2 and take it to a muffler shop for welding. <BR>if it has a compression fitting, it's REALLY easy.. there are like 6-8 springs that hold the thing up and how ever you took it off re-install it the same way. just use a hack saw and lop off the cat about 3" past the stock welding marks (on the passengerside!!). use the supplied clamp and make sure it's STOOPID tight and doens't leak before you put the car back down on the ground... cause if you put it down and it leaks you'll be frustrated and it'll leak for a month before you get it fixed...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> been there. <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstmeatsig.jpg">            <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 08-29-2001).]||||reg||1
